blocks.text:
The money leaves your account at the moment of purchase. {{1}}
All your purchases for the month appear together on one bill. {{2}}
You pay the purchase price in several instalments over weeks or months. {{3}}
Without funds in your account, the payment will usually not go through. {{4}}
The bank pays the money on your behalf – you are billed later. {{5}}
Popular in online shops: ‘Order now, pay in 30 days or in instalments.’ {{6}}
Your account balance shows your spending immediately. {{7}}
If you do not pay the monthly bill in full, you pay high interest. {{8}}
Lots of small instalments from different orders can easily add up unnoticed. {{9}}
